{
  "id": "scenario-04",
  "title": "Scenario 4 - GL, Auto, and Umbrella for Event Operations",
  "formType": "acord-25",
  "summary": "Coastal Event Group emails about a revised certificate for a festival venue. The venue's waiver-of-subrogation ask isn't something every policy on file actually has — read the endorsements carefully.",
  "instructions": [
    "Read the email from Coastal Event Group and check the waiver-of-subrogation request against each policy file below — don't assume it applies just because it was asked for.",
    "Complete the General Liability, Automobile Liability, and Umbrella sections using the policy files exactly as written.",
    "Use the exact remark wording required for the venue in the description of operations box.",
    "Leave Workers Compensation blank — there is no file for that coverage on this account.",
    "Set the revision number as the email describes."
  ],
  "request": [
    {
      "label": "Date",
      "lines": [
        "04/29/2026"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Client Email",
      "lines": [
        "From: Felix Tran, Managing Partner, Coastal Event Group, LLC <felix@coastaleventgroup.com>",
        "To: certificates@lavatraining.com",
        "Subject: Revised COI for Bayside Convention Center — Summer Festival",
        "Hi Ana,",
        "The Bayside Convention Center reviewed the certificate we sent for the 2026 Summer Food & Music Festival (June 14-16) and said it needs a revision number since we added the umbrella policy this year — please mark this as revision 1.",
        "The certificate holder is included as additional insured with respect to the named insured's event operations for the 2026 Summer Food & Music Festival held June 14-16, 2026.",
        "Their events coordinator also asked for a waiver of subrogation across all our policies — GL, auto, and umbrella — since that's apparently standard for their venue contracts. Let me know if that's something we already have.",
        "Also, just a reminder: we don't own any vehicles, our staff just drives rental vans and their own cars to haul equipment, so make sure the auto section reflects that.",
        "Thanks,",
        "Felix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Certificate Holder / Requestor",
